<!--meta {"lead": "HairPop is used on a phone in one hand while choosing a style. Every screen starts at 360px and gains columns, navigation and space as the viewport grows.", "description": "Mobile-first rules, breakpoints, what each component does at each width, touch and the testing matrix.", "covers": "Mobile-first rules, breakpoints, per-component behaviour, touch, safe areas, testing matrix"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Base styles target a 360px phone. Breakpoints only add: more columns, the top navigation links, centred dialogs, docked toasts. Nothing is designed desktop-first and squeezed down.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use <code>min-width</code> media queries only, written in <code>rem</code> (<code>48rem</code>, <code>64rem</code>) so they move with the person's font size. The mocks' <code>max-width: 47.99rem</code> overrides were rewritten mobile-first.</li>
    <li>Prefer tokens that already change with the viewport (<code>--layout-columns</code>, <code>--layout-gutter</code>, <code>--layout-margin</code>) over new queries.</li>
    <li>Custom properties cannot be used inside <code>@media</code>, so the breakpoint values are repeated there by convention; the canonical values are the <code>--layout-breakpoint-*</code> tokens on the <a href="layout.html">layout</a> page.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="breakpoints"><h2><a href="#breakpoints">Breakpoints</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Query</th><th scope="col">Width</th><th scope="col">What changes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>base</td><td>none</td><td>0–639px</td><td>4 columns, 16px gutter and margin; one-column content; bottom-sheet dialogs; full-width toasts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>sm</td><td><code>(min-width: 40rem)</code></td><td>640px</td><td>Dialogs centre with a 24px frame; toasts dock bottom right at 24rem; pagination summary sits inline.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>md</td><td><code>(min-width: 48rem)</code></td><td>768px</td><td>8 columns, 24px gutter, 32px margin; top-bar links appear; feature grid goes to 2 columns; detail grid gets its aside; forms may pair short fields; primary actions stop being full width.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>lg</td><td><code>(min-width: 64rem)</code></td><td>1024px</td><td>12 columns, 32px gutter, 48px margin; feature grid goes to 3 columns; sidebar navigation becomes persistent.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>xl</td><td><code>(min-width: 80rem)</code></td><td>1280px</td><td>Content reaches <code>--layout-container-max</code> and centres.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2xl</td><td><code>(min-width: 96rem)</code></td><td>1536px</td><td>Nothing new; margins absorb the extra width.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="components"><h2><a href="#components">Behaviour by component</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Component</th><th scope="col">Below the breakpoint</th><th scope="col">At and above</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/top-bar.html">Top bar</a></td><td>Brand, menu button (<code>.topbar__menu</code>, <code>aria-expanded</code>) and account links; primary links move into the menu (&lt; 768px)</td><td>Primary links inline in <code>.topbar__nav</code>; menu button hidden</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/dialog.html">Dialog</a></td><td>Full-width bottom sheet, top corners <code>--radius-xl</code>, sticky footer, safe-area padding (&lt; 640px)</td><td>Centred panel, <code>--radius-lg</code>, scales in</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/toast.html">Toast</a></td><td>Full width, 16px from each edge, above the safe area (&lt; 640px)</td><td>24rem column, bottom right, 24px inset</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/form-layout.html">Form layout</a></td><td>One column; primary action full width and first (&lt; 768px)</td><td>Short related fields (first and last name, date and time) may pair in <code>.form-row</code>; actions right-aligned</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/container.html">Feature grid</a></td><td>1 column</td><td>2 columns at 768px, 3 at 1024px</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/container.html">Detail grid</a></td><td>Main content, then the aside below it (&lt; 768px)</td><td>Main 2fr beside an aside of at least <code>--layout-sidebar-width</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/table.html">Table</a></td><td>Scrolls horizontally inside <code>.table-wrap</code>; never the page</td><td>Same; most tables fit</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/tabs.html">Tabs</a></td><td>Scroll horizontally; never wrap to two rows</td><td>Fit on one row</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/page-header.html">Page header</a></td><td>Actions move under the title; primary action full width (&lt; 768px)</td><td>Actions beside the title</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/pagination.html">Pagination</a></td><td>"Showing 1–3 of 126" on its own line above the page links (&lt; 640px)</td><td>Summary inline before the links</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/sidebar-navigation.html">Sidebar navigation</a></td><td>Hidden; opened as a drawer from the menu button (&lt; 1024px)</td><td>Persistent, sticky, <code>--layout-sidebar-width</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/description-list.html">Description list</a></td><td>Term above value (&lt; 640px)</td><td>Term and value side by side</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/avatar.html">Avatar</a> (profile)</td><td>48px</td><td>64px from 768px</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="../components/empty-state.html">Empty state</a></td><td>Title at the h3 size</td><td>Title at 28px from 768px</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Live preview at phone width</h3>
  <div class="ds-phone"><div class="ds-frame"><header class="topbar"><a class="topbar__brand" href="#overview">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="#overview">Maya</a></header><div class="ds-frame__body"><p class="eyebrow">Discover</p><h2>Find a style that feels like you</h2><div class="stack" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);"><label class="search-box"><span class="visually-hidden">Search styles (phone preview)</span><input class="input" type="search" value="knotless braids"></label><a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="#overview">Find braiders</a></div></div></div></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="type-and-space"><h2><a href="#type-and-space">Type and space</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Body and UI text use fixed steps from the type scale so they follow browser zoom. Only the display and h1 sizes are fluid, through <code>clamp()</code> inside <code>--font-size-4xl</code> and <code>--font-size-5xl</code>.</li>
    <li>Spacing never scales with viewport width; a breakpoint swaps the token (for example <code>--layout-margin</code> from 16 to 32 to 48px).</li>
    <li>Prose stays under <code>--layout-measure</code> (65 characters) at every width.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="usage"><h2><a href="#usage">Usage</a></h2>
  <h3>Touch and pointer</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Targets are at least 24×24px everywhere and 44px for a screen's primary mobile action, nav links and tabs. <code>(pointer: coarse)</code> is not used to grow targets; they are already large enough.</li>
    <li>Under <code>(hover: none)</code>, hover-only affordances (table row actions) are always visible.</li>
    <li>Nothing depends on hover alone: tooltips also open on focus, and every hover reveal has a tap or keyboard path.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Viewport edges</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Fixed bottom elements (bottom sheets, the toast region) add <code>env(safe-area-inset-bottom)</code> so the home indicator never covers an action.</li>
    <li>Full-height layouts use <code>100dvh</code>, so mobile browser toolbars do not clip the footer.</li>
    <li>No page scrolls horizontally at 320px; only tables, code and tab lists scroll inside their own wrappers.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Reflow (WCAG 1.4.10):</b> every screen works at 320 CSS px, which is 1280px at 400% zoom, without two-dimensional scrolling.</li>
    <li><b>Orientation (1.3.4):</b> nothing locks to portrait or landscape.</li>
    <li><b>Resize text (1.4.4):</b> sizes are in <code>rem</code>, so 200% text size enlarges everything and breakpoints follow.</li>
    <li><b>Focus not obscured (2.4.11):</b> the sticky top bar is matched by <code>scroll-padding-top</code>, so a focused field never hides beneath it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="testing"><h2><a href="#testing">Testing matrix</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Viewport</th><th scope="col">Represents</th><th scope="col">Check</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>360×800, light and dark</td><td>Phones</td><td>No horizontal scroll, dialogs are sheets, toasts span the width, primary action full width, menu button present.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>768×1024, light and dark</td><td>Tablets</td><td>Top-bar links appear, 2-column feature grid, detail aside beside main, dialogs centred.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>1280×800, light and dark</td><td>Laptops and desktops</td><td>3-column feature grid, container max reached, tables fit.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>1280 at 400% zoom</td><td>Low vision</td><td>Same as 360: everything reflows to one column.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <pre><code>python .claude/skills/writing-html-mocks/scripts/screenshot_mocks.py docs/mocks
python .claude/skills/writing-html-mocks/scripts/screenshot_mocks.py docs/design-system --out docs/design-system/.cache/shots</code></pre>
</section>
